rzmq 0.5.26: PUB never blocks on a subscriber whose queue is full.

ZMQ RFC 29 and libzmq: a PUB drops a message for a subscriber at its HWM and keeps
serving the others; zmq_send never blocks. rzmq's distributor instead awaited the full
subscriber per SNDTIMEO, and the default SNDTIMEO (-1) meant up to 30 s per message on
io_uring sessions (unbounded on Tokio sessions): one stalled subscriber stalled the
publisher and every other subscriber. Now a full subscriber misses the message unless
SNDTIMEO is explicitly positive, which keeps the wait-then-drop behaviour as an opt-in.

Tests: core/tests/pub_stalled_subscriber.rs (fails on 0.5.26 in both session modes).

